            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed both added files in full. CheckEvidence validates the shape of the record and every ref (review.ResultRef, review.VerdictRef) before locating the repository or touching the store, so a ref such as an absolute path or one that climbs out of the results directory is rejected without any read; evidence_test.go covers these cases and asserts that no git or store calls happen.",
              "File reads go through s.results.Read(repo.Root, feature, name) with feature and name taken from the validated ref parsers, and the doc comment says the store refuses links, non-regular files and paths leaving the results directory. No path is built from raw record input in this candidate.",
              "Digests are compared against the bytes stored now (review.CheckFile), and the range is checked against the stored binding (review.CheckRange), so a tampered or swapped result or verdict is refused. The function only reads and stores nothing.",
              "The new function adds no dependency, secret or network access. Non-review-report records return early, which keeps the behavior of other records unchanged. No reachable security, data exposure or data loss impact was found."
            ]
          }
        }
